\par   The Mic Gain controls the input level to the quadrature mixers and is the main control for adjusting the output power of the transmitter in the non compressed mode. It is important not to turn the mic gain up to high,
 as it is possible to overflow the DSP registers. When this happens extreme distortion occurs. In the case of an analog amplifier that is driven to hard, a sine wave input drives the amplifier into saturation and causes the result shown in fig 1. (flat to
pping). In the case of a DSP overflow the distortion is as shown in fig 2. Up to the point of overflow there is no distortion using DSP.
